The literal `11` is a magic number whose value depends on `THEME_COLOR_LIMIT - 1` from the theme layer. The CSS generator in `styles.ts` loops `for (let i = 0; i < THEME_COLOR_LIMIT; i++)` and emits `.section-${i - 1}`, so with `THEME_COLOR_LIMIT = 12` the valid non-root section classes are `section-0` through `section-10` — exactly 11 classes. The modulus must equal that count. If any theme ever changes `THEME_COLOR_LIMIT`, this hardcoded `11` will silently regress (producing out-of-range section numbers and the same black-node bug). At minimum, extract this into a named constant with an explanatory comment:
```ts
// Must stay in sync with THEME_COLOR_LIMIT - 1 in styles.ts:
// that loop generates section-0 through section-(THEME_COLOR_LIMIT-2)
const MINDMAP_SECTION_COUNT = 11;
const childSectionNumber = node.level === 0 ? index % MINDMAP_SECTION_COUNT : sectionNumber;
```
Ideally, read the value from the theme/config so the two files cannot drift.
